# KickFixApp — Codebase KT (Developer Handoff)

This document explains **what the KickFixApp repo is**, how the app works end-to-end, and what each important file/module does. It is intended to let a developer **continue development immediately** without needing prior context.

---

## 1) Project intent

**KickFix** is a React Native (CLI) mobile app for **real-time martial arts kick form feedback**.

At runtime, the app:

- streams **MediaPipe Pose** landmarks (33 landmarks per frame, **both image-space normalized AND world-space in meters**) from the device camera
- detects **kick onset** with a knee-velocity heuristic (was ankle-separation in v0)
- buffers `PoseFrame[]` during the kick (image + world + timestamp per frame)
- runs a kick-specific analyzer — **Front Snap** uses the new 19-criterion biomechanics engine; **Roundhouse / Side Kick** still use the legacy image-space port (to be migrated)
- displays **either a Quick HUD** (minimal score + verdict + cue) **or a Full Analysis review** (slow-mo skeleton replay + scrubber + full scorecard)
- tracks per-session stats (total / good kicks, FPS, streak)
- stores kick summaries (`kicks` table) and **landmark-only replays** (`kick_frames` table — never video)

The kick analysis logic in TypeScript was originally a port of the desktop reference implementation in `logic.py`, with thresholds adapted to **scale with body size in the frame** (so the app behaves similarly when the user is closer/farther from the camera). The Front Snap analyzer has since been **rewritten on top of MediaPipe world landmarks** for true rotation/scale-invariant biomechanics.

