## 10) Screens overview (what each screen does today)

### `src/screens/TrainSelectScreen.tsx`

Entry point for training. Shows greeting + "LET'S TRAIN AND GET BETTER" header. Three large kick cards with image assets. Tapping opens a bottom sheet to choose Quick or Full Analysis (or open a Technique Video stub).

### `src/screens/CameraScreen.tsx`

**Rewritten** for the new biomech engine. Live training screen:

- requests camera permission via `requestCameraPermission()`
- renders the MediaPipe landmark stream view
- knee-velocity onset detection + 5-frame pre-roll buffering
- runs `analyzeFrontSnap` after each kick (deferred via `InteractionManager`)
- HUD: top — mode pill, FPS, kick count, RECORDING indicator; bottom — big score number, verdict, headline cue
- Routes to `KickReview` for Full mode after each kick

### `src/screens/KickReviewScreen.tsx` (NEW)

Full Analysis post-kick review. See §6.3 for full layout. Slow-mo skeleton replay + scrubber + scorecard + NEXT KICK button.

### `src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx`

Final state — pure black bg, "YOUR STATS" h2, no streak counter. Stat cards: KICKS / ACCURACY / SESSIONS. Action buttons (Set Goals, Kick History) — white text, red icons.

### `src/screens/ProfileScreen.tsx`

Profile + settings hub. Shows username/email/belt level, links to Edit Username, Edit Profile, sign out.

### `src/screens/KickHistoryScreen.tsx`

Placeholder — wire up to read `kicks` rows and link into `KickReview` (planned).

### `src/screens/SetGoalsScreen.tsx`

Placeholder for goal-setting feature.

### Auth screens

- `SignInScreen.tsx`, `SignUpScreen.tsx`, `WelcomeScreen.tsx`
